# issue-flow command reference

This project uses **{{ editor_name }}**. {% if commands_supported %}The commands are **slash commands** under `{{ agent_dir }}/{{ commands_dir }}/`, mirrored by **Agent Skills** under `{{ agent_dir }}/skills/`.{% else %}The commands are **Agent Skills** under `{{ agent_dir }}/skills/`; they appear in the slash menu as `/iflow`, `/iflow-plan`, and friends.{% endif %} Paths on this page are for {{ editor_name }}; other editors use other folders (see [Editor support]({{ site }}/editors/)). Issue state is tracked in `{{ issueflows_dir }}/{{ current_issues_folder }}/`. The ideas behind the workflow (focus issue, on-path vs off-path, where the agent stops to ask) are explained in [Concepts]({{ site }}/concepts/).

> **Keyboard-friendly chat:** type **`iflow plan`**, **`iflow pick`**, **`iflow close`**, etc. in chat (letters + space only). Slash menu still uses `/iflow-plan`. Hyphen form `iflow-plan` also works. Norwegian and similar layouts often lack a dedicated `/` key; `@` is awkward too — the space form is intentional. Every command can be typed all three ways, for example `iflow plan`, `iflow-plan`, `/iflow-plan`.

**Quick start:** type **`iflow`** in chat or run **`/iflow`** from the slash menu. It inspects the state of the focus issue and dispatches to the right linear-flow {% if commands_supported %}command{% else %}skill{% endif %} (`iflow capture` / `/iflow-capture`, `iflow plan` / `/iflow-plan`, `iflow build` / `/iflow-build`, or `iflow close` / `/iflow-close`) — so you don't have to remember which step is next. Haven't chosen an issue yet? Start with **`iflow pick`** or **`/iflow-pick`**.
